<title>USA: Basic Petroleum to buy Guatemala stake.</title>
<headline>Basic Petroleum to buy Guatemala stake.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basic Petroleum International Ltd said Monday it agreed to acquire a 30 percent interest in Contract 1-91 in Guatemala's Central Peten for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>Contract 1-91 covers 42,000 acres and is held by Compania General de Combustibles, an Argentine subsidiary of Compania Comercial del Plata. The acquisition will be completed upon receipt of Guatemalan government approval.</p>
<p>Although not yet in production, three wells have been drilled and were successfully tested for oil.  During 1997, workovers of the three wells and a program of 200 kilometers of seismic are planned, Basic said.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
